It does not license any other file in this repository.

Game-derived content
--------------------
game.asm and bank_*.asm under asm/JP/ and asm/US/ contain disassemblies of
"Deja Vu I & II - The Casebooks of Ace Harding" (Japan and USA).
Rights in the original game's code, text, graphics, audio, and other data
remain with their respective rights
holders. This project grants no license to those materials or to ROMs
reconstructed from them.

Third-party hardware definitions
-------------------------------
asm/JP/hardware.inc and asm/US/hardware.inc are from gbdev/hardware.inc,
revision 225e671a9eb1f81c90e0cc17d29e59c6983657db (version 4.8.0).
Their contents match that revision apart from line endings.
Both files are covered by the upstream CC0 1.0 Universal dedication:
https://github.com/gbdev/hardware.inc/blob/225e671a9eb1f81c90e0cc17d29e59c6983657db/LICENSE
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode
The original contributor credits remain in both files.

External tools
--------------
The assembly files credit mgbdis v3.0 by Matt Currie and contributors.
mgbdis is licensed separately under MIT:
https://github.com/mattcurrie/mgbdis/blob/master/LICENSE
RGBDS is an external build dependency:
https://github.com/gbdev/rgbds
Tool licenses do not grant rights in the original game's content.

